AmxxRpc vendored patch: hlsdk/dlls/extdll.h — disable min/max macros on non-Windows

Reason:
  The non-Windows branch of extdll.h defines `min`/`max` function-like macros.
  They collide with libstdc++ headers (<algorithm>/<cmath>) pulled in later by
  amxxmodule.cpp / our sources, producing hard compile errors on Linux (-m32).
  `NOMINMAX` only affects the Windows branch and does not help here.

Fix:
  Comment out the `#ifndef min ... #endif` and `#ifndef max ... #endif` blocks
  (canonical approach used by Next21Team/AmxxEasyHttp's vendored halflife).

Apply (from repo root):
  patch -p1 < third_party/patches/hlsdk-extdll-minmax.patch

